be able to do that innately without relying on having the ring with them I\u2019d allow the players to Scrutinize the ring, and after they\u2019ve gotten through the Opacity they can pay one XP for a special attainment they can turn on at any time when using Mage Sight to give themselves Ring Mage Sight. Considering the ring\u2019s origin I\u2019d consider also having the use of ring sight accrue Notice.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, and maybe more interesting, instead of modifying existing Mage Sight, I\u2019d treat it as a completely different Mage Sight altogether. Use that to Scrutinize the ring successfully, pay an XP and you just innately have it. As you gather each piece of the regalia I\u2019d give the option to increase your Ring Sight \u201carcana\u201d which doesn\u2019t give any magic, but does increase your safe rolls, and dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T09:15:29-07:00","id":1336057,"title":"","content":"So, Signs of Sorcery contains the section about Seer reward artifacts, which contains my party line - the Ring is an Artifact that allows the wielder to access an unusual form of Mage Sight. There is some precedent - Joined Scelesti have their Mage Sight warped so they see their Dur-Abzu rather than their old Path. I just figure Ring Sight shows a landscape tuned entirely to the influence of the Exarchs and nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/mem